"```json\n{\n  \"critic_suggestions\": \"1. **Text Clipping in Evaluation Block (Critical)**: The rightmost box ('Evaluation on the same 5 observations') has insufficient horizontal width, causing the right border to visibly clip the text on multiple lines (the 's' in 'observations' is truncated to 'observation', and the 'k' in 'arithmetic check' collides with or is clipped by the right border). The node width must be expanded (to ~4.0\u20134.2 cm) with adequate inner margins (`inner xsep=6pt`) so that all lines render completely without clipping.\\n2. **Annotation Placement**: The italic note 'data dependency: correction computed from observed residuals' currently hangs directly under the 'Residuals' box. It should be centered cleanly underneath the horizontal arrow connecting 'Residuals' to the scalar correction box '$b$', which directly highlights the dependency relationship between those two stages.\\n3. **Horizontal Spacing**: The spacing between the scalar correction box ($b$) and the 'Corrected prediction' box is somewhat compressed, leaving very little room for the '$+b$' arrow and label. Increasing the gap between Column 3 and Column 4 by at least 0.4\u20130.6 cm will improve visual breathing room and readability.\",\n  \"revised_description\": \"**Figure description: `fig_residual_workflow` (diagram, LaTeX/TikZ)**\\n\\n**Canvas and style**\\n- Pure white background, no outer frame border, no drop shadows, no gradients.\\n- Landscape canvas, dimensions approximately 17 cm \u00d7 7.5 cm, laid out strictly from left to right across 5 non-overlapping horizontal stages with generous spacing to avoid collisions and clipping.\\n- All text and math in Computer Modern: 8\u20139 pt for annotations, 9\u201310 pt for node labels, 10 pt for mathematical symbols.\\n- Rounded rectangular nodes with 3 pt corner radius, 0.6 pt outline, and light thematic fills:\\n  - Observations: pale blue fill `#DDEBF7`, outline `#2F5597`.\\n  - Baseline predictor: light gray fill `#EFEFEF`, outline `#595959`.\\n  - Residuals & scalar correction: pale orange fill `#FBE5D6`, outline `#C55A11`.\\n  - Corrected prediction: pale green fill `#E2F0D9`, outline `#548235`.\\n  - Evaluation: white fill, dark gray outline `#404040`.\\n- Arrows:\\n  - Solid computation/dependency arrows: 0.8 pt line width, dark gray `#333333`, `-Stealth` tips.\\n  - Dashed reuse path: 0.6 pt dashed (3 pt on, 2 pt off), color `#2F5597`, routed along the bottom row.\\n\\n**Layout and elements (strictly non-overlapping, left to right)**\\n\\n1. **Observation block (Column 1, centered vertically)**\\n   - A tall rounded box labeled 'Observations ($n = 5$)' at the top.\\n   - Contains a minimal two-column table:\\n     - Header: $x$ and $y = 2x+3$ separated by a horizontal rule.\\n     - Rows: $(-2, -1), (-1, 1), (0, 3), (1, 5), (2, 7)$.\\n   - Keep width around 3.0 cm so it clears subsequent columns comfortably.\\n\\n2. **Baseline predictor (Column 2, upper row)**\\n   - Positioned horizontally to the right of the Observation block (clearing its right border by at least 0.8 cm) and vertically aligned above the Residuals block.\\n   - Box labeled 'Fixed baseline' with $\\\\hat{y}^{(0)} = 2x$.\\n   - Direct incoming solid arrow with right-angle step from the Observation block to the baseline box, labeled '$x$'.\\n\\n3. **Residual computation (Column 2, lower row)**\\n   - Pale orange box positioned directly below the Baseline predictor box with clear vertical separation (~0.8 cm).\\n   - Labeled 'Residuals' with formula $r_i = y_i - 2x_i$.\\n   - Displays computed values: $r_i = 3, 3, 3, 3, 3$ ($i=1,\\\\dots,5$).\\n   - Incoming solid horizontal arrow from the Observation block (labeled '$y_i$') and a vertical solid arrow from the Fixed baseline box above (labeled '$2x_i$').\\n\\n4. **Scalar correction (Column 3, vertically centered with Residuals)**\\n   - Pale orange box placed strictly to the right of the Residuals box (clearing it with a 1.0 cm gap).\\n   - Contains formula $b = \\\\frac{1}{5}\\\\sum_{i=1}^{5} r_i = 3$.\\n   - Incoming horizontal arrow from Residuals to $b$.\\n   - Centered directly beneath this connecting arrow, the key annotation: 'data dependency: correction computed from observed residuals' in 8 pt italic text, with sufficient vertical clearance from both the box and the bottom reuse dashed line.\\n\\n5. **Corrected prediction (Column 4, vertically centered)**\\n   - Pale green box placed strictly to the right of Column 3 with at least 1.0 cm horizontal clearance.\\n   - Labeled 'Corrected prediction' with formula $\\\\hat{y}_i = 2x_i + b$.\\n   - Incoming arrow 1: A route from the top of the Fixed baseline box running horizontally above Column 3 and descending into the top of the Corrected prediction box, labeled '$2x_i$'.\\n   - Incoming arrow 2: Horizontal solid arrow from the scalar correction box $b$ to the left edge of Corrected prediction, labeled '$+b$' centered clearly above the arrow.\\n\\n6. **Evaluation block (Column 5, far right, vertically centered)**\\n   - White rounded box placed strictly to the right of Corrected prediction with clear separation (at least 1.0 cm gap).\\n   - Generous box width (minimum 4.0\u20134.2 cm) with `inner xsep=6pt` to ensure zero text collision or border clipping:\\n     - Title: 'Evaluation on the same 5 observations' (fully visible without truncating 'observations').\\n     - Math: $e_i = \\\\hat{y}_i - y_i = 0$ (centered on a single line).\\n     - Note: 'finite arithmetic check, not generalization' (fully visible without clipping 'check' against the right border).\\n   - Direct horizontal solid arrow from the right edge of Corrected prediction to the left edge of Evaluation.\\n   - Dashed blue reuse arrow originating from the bottom center of the Observation block, dropping into a dedicated lower corridor below all blocks, and entering the bottom of the Evaluation block. Labeled along the horizontal segment: 'same observations reused' in 8 pt blue text.\\n\\n**Output format notes**\\n- Native editable `.tex` source ensuring coordinate/node positioning (`right=of ...`, `above=of ...`) with explicit bounding box and node widths preventing any text clipping or overlaps.\\n- Vector PDF and 300 dpi raster preview.\"\n}\n```"